{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>My soul longeth</b> — It desired, and nearly expired from the intensity of desire. The meaning: it transgressed the boundary of desire; therefore the word 'also' (gam)." "<b>For the courts of YHWH</b> — If this is by the sons of Korah, it is in Babylonia; or if by the sons of Korah, in the days of David." "<b>For the courts</b> — That is, the surroundings of the Tent of HaShem; or by way of prophecy." "<b>My heart</b> — It is the intellect and knowledge, which are in the soul." "<b>And my flesh</b> — The body; and 'the bird' (שער) — the mouth. Meaning: the bird of the body's flesh sings, along with the intellect's thought of everything — it is the mouth, which is the opening of the body; therefore it sings." "<b>And the sense of El</b> — Corresponding to 'expired'; or that the living creature, the heart, was together with the flesh."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 84, :notes {1 "The repetition of 'the sons of Korah' is literal; the comment distinguishes between a late exilic author and an early Davidic-era author.", 4 "Ibn Ezra appears to read שיר as שער or treats the lemma as requiring a homonym note; the hyper-literal rendering preserves the textual difficulty without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:01.628014447Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}